From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: PS3RECOMP_VK_VALIDATION=1, the validation layer and a
 debug messenger with per-ID counts

Off by default. With PS3RECOMP_VK_VALIDATION=1 the instance enables
VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation when the loader lists it, and
VK_EXT_debug_utils (from the loader or the layer) with a messenger for
errors and warnings (general, validation and performance) that writes to
the log. A frame repeats one mistake hundreds of times, so messages are
keyed by their ID (their name when the ID is 0, as some driver and loader
messages have): the first 3 of a key are logged in full, then one line at
10, 100, 1000... occurrences, and the counts of every key are listed,
most frequent first, when the backend shuts down or the process exits.
The filter and the switch's parser are in rsx_vk_debug.h, plain C a host
test can include alone.

A missing layer or extension is logged and the run goes on without it;
if vkCreateInstance fails with them, it is tried again without, before the
existing fallbacks (temporal upscaler's extensions, then the surface's).
The layer can also come from the loader
(VK_LOADER_LAYERS_ENABLE='*validation*'); this switch adds the
messenger and the counts. Written from the Vulkan specification and the
validation layer's documentation.

The layer itself stops reporting an ID after 10 by default; when it offers
VK_EXT_layer_settings, its enable_message_limit is turned off so the counts
at quit are the true ones.
